.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-015-goal-subgoals.md:120:### Completion and audit semantics
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-015-goal-subgoals.md:122:- Parent completion is refused if any blocking subgoal is `pending`, `active`, `failed`, or `blocked` without explicit escalation evidence.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-015-goal-subgoals.md:123:- Accepted terminal states for a blocking subgoal are:
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-015-goal-subgoals.md:126:- Subgoal progress counts are advisory. They must not replace qualitative completion audit or durable proof gates.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-015-goal-subgoals.md:127:- Future `/goal audit` should incorporate subgoal state, but parent completion must be deterministically blocked even without `/goal audit`.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-015-goal-subgoals.md:131:- `get_goal` and related tool output should summarize current child, status, and blockers.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-015-goal-subgoals.md:132:- The footer/widget should show a compact child row such as `subgoal 1/3 active: clean dirty worktree` when subgoals exist.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-015-goal-subgoals.md:133:- Detailed subgoal lists belong in tool output, not in the narrow widget.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-015-goal-subgoals.md:134:- No-subgoal goals should render exactly as before.
